{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"LEAF 0880 floaty-imperfect-pomeranian — COMPLETE AND PUSHED. Gerrit 2507, commit 07b3051f1a3f,\n11 files / 1247 insertions. https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2507\nShips: 3 reports under reports/stability/, ADR 0110 + .numbers/0110 + regenerated index, and an\n--all-work mode on scripts/backtest_bugfix_size.py (442 -> 496 lines) with the heavy logic extracted\nto scripts/_backtest/{all_work,stats}.py. The package (not a flat sibling module) was chosen because\ncheck_import_walk.py imports every top-level scripts/*.py standalone with the scripts dir stripped\nfrom sys.path; a subpackage is invisible to that walk. Import walk passes 75/75.\n\nAC2 VERIFIED BY ACTUALLY RUNNING THE DOCUMENTED COMMAND, not by assertion:\n  python scripts/backtest_bugfix_size.py --all-work --rev-range origin/main\n    --since 2026-07-01 --until 2026-09-02 --out reports/stability/change-shape-backtest.json\nreproduces every published figure — 2207 commits in window, corpus 1795, non_test_lines mean 214.1\np90 487.2 max 7228, files_union mean 6.8 p90 13, histogram {1:1617,2:121,3:34,4:19,6:1,7:2,25:1},\nrho vs files +0.370 (p=4.3e-42), caused_by vs files +0.190 (p=2.7e-16), >150 n=689 at 12.9%.\nAC7 preserved: all_work.py imports BUGFIX_SIZE_THRESHOLD_NON_TEST_LINES, count_non_test_diff_lines\nand is_test_path from the shipped gate and re-derives none; threshold_split uses the constant, never\na literal 150. --check-planning-corpus still PASSES (113/113 pin, exit 0).\n\nTHE SUBAGENT FOUND A REAL BUG IN THE DRAFT ANALYSIS AND REFUSED TO TUNE IT AWAY — exactly what I\nasked for. The published corpus of 1,793 came from a resolution universe admitting a ticket only if\nit had a gate event or a 19-CHARACTER store directory. Jira-bridged tickets are named like\n'jira-reb-596', so they entered only by accident: jira-reb-1163 WAS counted (it happened to carry a\nCOMPLETION_VERDICT) while jira-reb-596 and jira-reb-687 were NOT, though all three have commits in\nthe window. Enumerating every ticket directory is the consistent rule and gives 1,795. It shipped no\nbug-compatibility switch. I corrected the report's affected cells (corpus n, two histogram buckets,\nthe threshold split, ticket LOC mean/p90) and wrote the correction and its cause INTO the report, so\na later reader sees why the number moved. Nothing the argument rests on changed: every rho, both\ngate-round n's and both caused_by rates are identical.\n\nSTACK NOW FIVE DEEP:\n 2503 (8ce5 parity) -> 2504 (f9b9 mirrors) -> 2505 (b0ac atomic) -> 2506 (15f2 guard) -> 2507 (0880)\nPENDING AMENDS still uncommitted in the worktree, deliberately kept separate from the 0880 commit:\n - 2503: co_names parity extension + facade fall-open + the make-lint stub in\n   test_check_criteria_vocabulary.py\n - 2506: the guard selection-scoping fix\nBoth need a stacked amend (checkout the target commit, amend, rebase the rest onto it), since a\nfollow-up commit would open a NEW Gerrit change rather than a new patchset."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788322561359528001,"uuid":"7677250d-d4c3-42eb-b5b0-b7db7aa8dbf5"}